[11.2,"o","\u001b[1;1H\u001b[0;1m* Lesson 1: the outline\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[2;1H\u001b[0mAn org file is an outline: a line that starts with stars is a headline,\u001b[K\u001b[3;1H\u001b[0mand the number of stars is its level. Everything under a headline, up to\u001b[K\u001b[4;1H\u001b[0mthe next one of the same or a higher level, is its subtree.\u001b[K\u001b[5;1H\u001b[K\u001b[6;1H\u001b[0m** 1.1 Fold and unfold\u001b[K\u001b[7;1H\u001b[0mPut the cursor on the \u001b[0;38;2;179;246;192m=Kitchen=\u001b[0m headline below and press \u001b[0;38;2;179;246;192m=<Tab>=\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[8;1H\u001b[0ma few times: it cycles the subtree between folded, its children and\u001b[K\u001b[9;1H\u001b[0meverything. \u001b[0;38;2;179;246;192m=<S-Tab>=\u001b[0m does the same for the whole file (press\u001b[K\u001b[10;1H\u001b[0mit until everything shows again).\u001b[K\u001b[11;1H\u001b[K\u001b[12;1H\u001b[0mThere is nothing to check here: move on when you are done.\u001b[K\u001b[13;1H\u001b[K\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0;38;2;166;219;255m*** Kitchen\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0;1m**** Pots\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0mTwo big ones and a small one.\u001b[K\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0;1m**** Pans\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0mA frying pan.\u001b[K\u001b[19;1H\u001b[K\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0m** 1.2 Insert a headline \u001b[0;38;2;255;192;185m ✗\u001b[0m\u001b[K\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0mPut the cursor on \u001b[0;38;2;179;246;192m=Apples=\u001b[0m and press \u001b[0;38;2;179;246;192m=<M-CR>=\u001b[0m: a new headline\u001b[K\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0mSHOW ALL                                                                        \u001b[K\u001b[1;1H"]
